[
  {
    "id": "g-reflexive",
    "title": "levanto-me",
    "summary": "reflexive verbs: get up, go to bed, be called",
    "intro": [
      "Some verbs come with a small word that points back to the person doing it: levantar-se (to get up, literally \"to raise oneself\").",
      "In Portugal that small word normally goes after the verb, joined with a hyphen: levanto-me (I get up).",
      "The small words are me, te, se, nos, se. With nós, the verb drops its -s: levantamos + nos = levantamo-nos."
    ],
    "tables": [
      { "verb": "levantar-se", "meaning": "to get up", "rows": [
        { "person": "eu", "form": "levanto-me" },
        { "person": "tu", "form": "levantas-te" },
        { "person": "ele / ela / você", "form": "levanta-se" },
        { "person": "nós", "form": "levantamo-nos" },
        { "person": "eles / elas / vocês", "form": "levantam-se" }
      ] }
    ],
    "examples": [
      { "pt": "Levanto-me às sete.", "en": "I get up at seven." },
      { "pt": "Deitamo-nos tarde.", "en": "We go to bed late." },
      { "pt": "Sinto-me cansado.", "en": "I feel tired." },
      { "pt": "Como te chamas?", "en": "What's your name?" }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "With não, and after question words such as como, onde or a que horas, the small word moves in front: Não me levanto cedo. Como te chamas? There's a full topic on this later.",
      "Starting a sentence with the small word (Me levanto…) sounds Brazilian. In Portugal: Levanto-me…",
      "Common ones: chamar-se (to be called), levantar-se, deitar-se (to go to bed), sentar-se (to sit down), sentir-se (to feel), esquecer-se de (to forget), lembrar-se de (to remember).",
      "Sentir changes in the eu form: sinto-me."
    ],
    "drills": [
      { "type": "form", "verb": "levantar-se", "person": "eu", "answer": "levanto-me" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "deitar-se", "person": "tu", "answer": "deitas-te" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "chamar-se", "person": "ela", "answer": "chama-se" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "levantar-se", "person": "nós", "answer": "levantamo-nos" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "sentar-se", "person": "eles", "answer": "sentam-se" },
      { "type": "form", "verb": "sentir-se", "person": "eu", "answer": "sinto-me" },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "levantar-se", "before": "Eu ", "after": " às sete.", "answer": "levanto-me", "en": "I get up at seven." },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "levantar-se", "before": "A que horas te ", "after": "?", "answer": "levantas", "en": "What time do you get up?" },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "chamar-se", "before": "Ela ", "after": " Marta.", "answer": "chama-se", "en": "Her name is Marta." },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "deitar-se", "before": "Nós ", "after": " tarde ao sábado.", "answer": "deitamo-nos", "en": "We go to bed late on Saturdays." },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "esquecer-se", "before": "Eu ", "after": " sempre das chaves.", "answer": "esqueço-me", "en": "I always forget my keys." },
      { "type": "sentence", "verb": "sentir-se", "before": "Eu não me ", "after": " bem.", "answer": "sinto", "en": "I don't feel well." }
    ],
    "verified": false
  },
  {
    "id": "g-estar-a",
    "title": "estar a + verb",
    "summary": "what's happening right now",
    "intro": [
      "To say what's happening right now, Portugal uses estar + a + the verb in its dictionary form: Estou a trabalhar = I'm working.",
      "Only estar changes (estou, estás, está, estamos, estão). The second verb stays as it is."
    ],
    "examples": [
      { "pt": "Estou a trabalhar.", "en": "I'm working." },
      { "pt": "O que estás a fazer?", "en": "What are you doing?" },
      { "pt": "Está a chover.", "en": "It's raining." },
      { "pt": "Estou a aprender português.", "en": "I'm learning Portuguese." }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Brazil says estou trabalhando instead. In Portugal that sounds Brazilian, although you'll hear it in parts of the south (Alentejo, Algarve).",
      "It also covers things going on around now, not just this second: Estou a aprender português."
    ],
    "drills": [
      { "type": "sentence", "hint": "trabalhar", "before": "Eu ", "after": " agora.", "answer": "estou a trabalhar", "en": "I'm working now." },
      { "type": "sentence", "hint": "fazer, tu", "before": "O que ", "after": "?", "answer": "estás a fazer", "en": "What are you doing?" },
      { "type": "sentence", "hint": "ver", "before": "Nós ", "after": " um filme.", "answer": "estamos a ver", "en": "We're watching a film." },
      { "type": "sentence", "hint": "brincar", "before": "Os miúdos ", "after": " no jardim.", "answer": "estão a brincar", "en": "The kids are playing in the garden." },
      { "type": "sentence", "hint": "falar", "before": "A Ana ", "after": " ao telefone.", "answer": "está a falar", "en": "Ana is on the phone." },
      { "type": "sentence", "hint": "aprender", "before": "Eu ", "after": " português.", "answer": "estou a aprender", "en": "I'm learning Portuguese." },
      { "type": "sentence", "hint": "ouvir, tu", "before": "", "after": "?", "answer": "Estás a ouvir", "en": "Are you listening?" },
      { "type": "sentence", "hint": "jantar", "before": "Eles ", "after": ".", "answer": "estão a jantar", "en": "They're having dinner." },
      { "type": "sentence", "hint": "chover", "before": "", "after": ".", "answer": "Está a chover", "en": "It's raining." },
      { "type": "choice", "before": "Agora não posso, ", "after": ".", "options": ["estou a comer", "estou comendo"], "answer": "estou a comer", "en": "I can't right now, I'm eating.", "why": "Estou comendo is how Brazil says it. In Portugal: estou a comer." },
      { "type": "choice", "before": "O que ", "after": " a fazer?", "options": ["estás", "és"], "answer": "estás", "en": "What are you doing?", "why": "It's always estar a + verb." },
      { "type": "choice", "before": "O bebé ", "after": " a dormir.", "options": ["está", "é"], "answer": "está", "en": "The baby is sleeping.", "why": "It's always estar a + verb." }
    ],
    "verified": false
  },
  {
    "id": "g-verb-patterns",
    "title": "tenho de, costumo, preciso de",
    "summary": "verbs that team up with another verb",
    "focus": "word",
    "intro": [
      "Some verbs team up with a second verb, which stays in its dictionary form. Often there's a small word in between (de or a), and it's worth learning together with the verb."
    ],
    "tables": [
      { "verb": "patterns", "caption": "Verb + verb patterns", "listen": "form", "rows": [
        { "person": "have to", "form": "tenho de sair" },
        { "person": "usually", "form": "costumo jantar cedo" },
        { "person": "need to", "form": "preciso de dormir" },
        { "person": "start to", "form": "começo a perceber" },
        { "person": "do again", "form": "volto a ligar" },
        { "person": "stop doing", "form": "deixo de fumar" }
      ] }
    ],
    "examples": [
      { "pt": "Tenho de ir embora.", "en": "I have to go." },
      { "pt": "Costumo almoçar ao meio-dia.", "en": "I usually have lunch at midday." },
      { "pt": "Preciso de descansar.", "en": "I need to rest." },
      { "pt": "Volto a ligar mais tarde.", "en": "I'll call again later." }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Costumar has no English match. It's the everyday way to say \"usually\": Costumo ir a pé = I usually walk.",
      "Portugal keeps the de after precisar: preciso de sair, preciso de ajuda. Brazil often drops it before a verb.",
      "Gostar always takes de too: Gosto de nadar."
    ],
    "drills": [
      { "type": "sentence", "hint": "have to", "before": "Eu ", "after": " sair cedo.", "answer": "tenho de", "en": "I have to leave early." },
      { "type": "sentence", "hint": "have to", "before": "Eles ", "after": " trabalhar amanhã.", "answer": "têm de", "en": "They have to work tomorrow." },
      { "type": "sentence", "hint": "usually", "before": "Nós ", "after": " jantar às oito.", "answer": "costumamos", "en": "We usually have dinner at eight." },
      { "type": "sentence", "hint": "usually", "before": "Tu ", "after": " ir ao ginásio?", "answer": "costumas", "en": "Do you usually go to the gym?" },
      { "type": "sentence", "hint": "need to", "before": "Eu ", "after": " descansar.", "answer": "preciso de", "en": "I need to rest." },
      { "type": "sentence", "hint": "começar …", "before": "Ela começa ", "after": " trabalhar às nove.", "answer": "a", "en": "She starts work at nine." },
      { "type": "sentence", "hint": "voltar …", "before": "Volto ", "after": " ligar mais tarde.", "answer": "a", "en": "I'll call again later." },
      { "type": "sentence", "hint": "deixar …", "before": "Vou deixar ", "after": " fumar.", "answer": "de", "en": "I'm going to stop smoking." },
      { "type": "choice", "before": "", "after": "", "options": ["Preciso de ajuda.", "Preciso ajuda."], "answer": "Preciso de ajuda.", "en": "I need help.", "why": "Portugal keeps the de after precisar." },
      { "type": "choice", "before": "Gosto ", "after": " nadar.", "options": ["de", "a"], "answer": "de", "en": "I like swimming.", "why": "Gostar always takes de." },
      { "type": "choice", "before": "Começo ", "after": " perceber.", "options": ["a", "de"], "answer": "a", "en": "I'm starting to understand.", "why": "Começar takes a." },
      { "type": "choice", "before": "Tenho ", "after": " ir.", "options": ["de", "a"], "answer": "de", "en": "I have to go.", "why": "Ter de = to have to." }
    ],
    "verified": false
  },
  {
    "id": "g-ficar",
    "title": "ficar",
    "summary": "to stay, to be (for places), to become",
    "intro": [
      "Ficar is a regular -ar verb and one of the most useful in Portugal. It has several meanings:",
      "to stay (Fico em casa), to be somewhere for places that don't move (Onde fica o museu?), to become or get (Fica nervosa = she gets nervous), and ficar com = to take or keep (Fico com este = I'll take this one)."
    ],
    "table": [
      { "person": "eu", "form": "fico" },
      { "person": "tu", "form": "ficas" },
      { "person": "ele / ela / você", "form": "fica" },
      { "person": "nós", "form": "ficamos" },
      { "person": "eles / elas / vocês", "form": "ficam" }
    ],
    "examples": [
      { "pt": "Hoje fico em casa.", "en": "I'm staying at home today." },
      { "pt": "Onde fica o museu?", "en": "Where is the museum?" },
      { "pt": "Ela fica nervosa antes dos exames.", "en": "She gets nervous before exams." },
      { "pt": "Fico com este, obrigado.", "en": "I'll take this one, thanks." }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Fica para a próxima! = Maybe next time!",
      "Fica-te bem = it suits you (clothes, a haircut)."
    ],
    "drills": [
      { "type": "form", "person": "eu", "answer": "fico" },
      { "type": "form", "person": "tu", "answer": "ficas" },
      { "type": "form", "person": "ela", "answer": "fica" },
      { "type": "form", "person": "nós", "answer": "ficamos" },
